# COUNTIFS takes `(range, criteria)+` — an EVEN argument count, with no sum range.
# `calc_ifs` is shared with SUMIFS, which has an odd count because it leads with
# the range to sum, and it consumed that leading range unconditionally. So every
# well-formed COUNTIFS failed the arity check and returned an error, while
# COUNTIF, SUMIF and SUMIFS all worked.
INPUT A1 L1
INPUT B1 10
INPUT A2 L2
INPUT B2 20
INPUT A3 L1
INPUT B3 30

INPUT D1 =COUNTIFS(A1:A3,"L1")
CHECKNUM D1 2

INPUT D2 =COUNTIFS(A1:A3,"L2")
CHECKNUM D2 1

INPUT D3 =COUNTIFS(A1:A3,"L9")
CHECKNUM D3 0

# Two conditions: L1 rows whose hours exceed 15 — only the third row.
INPUT D4 =COUNTIFS(A1:A3,"L1",B1:B3,">15")
CHECKNUM D4 1

# Numeric conditions on their own.
INPUT D5 =COUNTIFS(B1:B3,">=20")
CHECKNUM D5 2

# Agrees with COUNTIF, which was never broken.
INPUT D6 =COUNTIF(A1:A3,"L1")-COUNTIFS(A1:A3,"L1")
CHECKNUM D6 0

# And with the SUMIFS it shares its machinery with.
INPUT D7 =SUMIFS(B1:B3,A1:A3,"L1")
CHECKNUM D7 40
